#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063964 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/id #uuid "4f78dc34-7cc7-5024-9641-b4ea74e4d155" :question/math-academy-id "e-3743" :question/problem "Find the $x$-values of the stationary points of $f(x) =  x^4 - 8 x ^ 2 + 2$ and classify each point." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x) = x^4 - 8 x ^ 2 + 2,$ we get\n\n$$\nf'(x)  = 4x^3 - 16 x,\n$$\n\nand solving $f'(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-16x & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}-4x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ x(x+2)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have stationary points at $x=0$ and $x=\\pm 2.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of $f''(x)$ at the critical points. Computing $f''(x),$ we get\n\n$$\nf''(x)= 12 x^2 - 16,\n$$\n\nand evaluating $f''(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-2) & =12(-2)^{2}-16=32>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =12(0)^{2}-16=-16<0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(2) & =12(2)^{2}-16=32>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=0,$ so this is a relative maximum. On the other hand, the second derivative is positive at $x=\\pm 2,$ so these are relative minima."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063965 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/id #uuid "088bc8a4-e82a-586b-89b5-49482f579c4d" :question/math-academy-id "e-3744" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x) = x^3-6x^2-15x.$ Given that $f'(5) = 0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f''(5)  >           0$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=5$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=5$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=5$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=  x^3-6x^2-15x,$ we get\n\n$$\nf'(x) =  3x^2-12x-15\n$$\n\nWe're given that $f'(5) = 0.$ Indeed, we can see that $f'(5) = 3(5)^2 - 12(5) - 15 = 0.$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =6x-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(5) & =6(5)-12 \\\\  & =30-12 \\\\  & =18>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is positive, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a38dba5-622e-5356-bae0-ac479825ebd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293836} {:answer/id #uuid "be64c842-1c2a-5e23-a999-aa07cfad96f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293837} {:answer/id #uuid "5c808dd9-e862-5d77-b630-69b56e7db2f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293838} {:answer/id #uuid "381f926c-73d2-55a8-b374-e171f87db6f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293839} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf16a51-e154-5a7d-95d8-b1d2a62fdb49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a38dba5-622e-5356-bae0-ac479825ebd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293836} :answer-field/id #uuid "f29de4f2-d3d7-5c89-9a1e-6f0bd70b60fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "625bbe54-0b3f-5afb-b15e-eb3a5b309cd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-114415" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=(1-x+{x}^{2}){e}^{x},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=0$\n- ${f}^{″}(0)>0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1$" :question/worked-solution "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=(1-x+{x}^{2}){e}^{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=(1-x+{x}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{x}+(-1+2x){e}^{x}=({x}^{2}+x){e}^{x},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+x){e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ x(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=-1,0.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=({x}^{2}+x)\\cdot {e}^{x}+(2x+1){e}^{x}=({x}^{2}+3x+1){e}^{x},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1) & =-{e}^{-1}<0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =1>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statements I and II are true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so there is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statements III is false. $x=1$ is not a critical point.\n\n- Statement IV is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19740fc7-c059-56b6-9990-723f7ddf5bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061603} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea47769-4dd7-5ccd-a76a-54f114fca891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061604} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe77206-a1c3-5167-ac5f-f8ec0d636c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061605} {:answer/id #uuid "7940920f-a322-5c3e-83f9-9af4d83c10bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061606} {:answer/id #uuid "7e85a37e-a2e2-5378-8b9d-19b70fd91053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19740fc7-c059-56b6-9990-723f7ddf5bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061603} :answer-field/id #uuid "2914e507-bc98-5466-90ad-8f67bf2f439d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061602}] :question/id #uuid "1fa08ecc-691c-5923-94fb-19ce5c958e14" :question/math-academy-id "q-21502" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nFor the function $f(x) = 2x^{3} - 6x + 12$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $x =-1$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n2. $f^{″}(-1) < 0$\n3. $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x =-1$" :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b24d93a5-c574-502e-8b49-eee4a7af58ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061612} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b4770d-54e4-55f5-8740-7594e0bbff53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061613} {:answer/id #uuid "09598d53-a609-5cbb-9cdc-1e6de3deaf3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061614} {:answer/id #uuid "0ebe97ff-1a3f-5ecc-80c2-7a6b3e2fcb6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061615} {:answer/id #uuid "5e9b87bb-d8c3-5c16-aa4b-838856c63fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09598d53-a609-5cbb-9cdc-1e6de3deaf3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061614} :answer-field/id #uuid "0907ab69-0c09-5e8b-b4dd-16f7323769d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061611}] :question/id #uuid "13f8cc2a-4183-5051-a10e-eea4f7de407e" :question/math-academy-id "q-21528" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nConsider the function $f(x) = x^{5} + 5x^{3} - 90x + 108$. Given that $f^{′}(-\\sqrt{3}) = 0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $f^{″}(-\\sqrt{3}) < 0$\n2. $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x =-\\sqrt{3}$\n3. $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x =-\\sqrt{3}$" :question/requires-calculator true}]}
